{
  "note": "The interface skin (docs/ART_DIRECTION.md; ui/play/ui_skin.gd, checked by UiSkin.validate in tools/check_data.gd): the palette, the sizes of the pieces and the contrast figures. It skins what is drawn as a pane over the open world on a desktop-sized window; a touch screen or a compact window keeps the older look. `pixel` is the size of one pixel of the skin's art in UI units (the world's pixel at the default zoom); the pieces are made at that size and drawn at whole multiples, never smoothed. Each `variants` entry is a full palette; `high_contrast` is the one the accessibility option picks. `contrast` lists pairs of palette names with the least contrast ratio each must keep in every variant (`min_hc` for the high-contrast variant, which may ask for more). `text_maps` says which palette colour stands in for the colours the dark overlay look uses (by hex) where a label sits on a parchment or a wood face.",
